cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  No Persistent Edge: A Pre-Registered, Multi-Phase Study of Retail
  Algorithmic Trading on Binance Spot (2017–2026)
message: >-
  If you use this software or its findings, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Cristhian
    family-names: Benitez
abstract: >-
  A self-funded, pre-registered research program evaluating whether any
  simple, retail-accessible algorithmic strategy has a persistent,
  exploitable edge on Binance Spot, net of realistic costs. Across six
  phases and 9.25 years of data (trend-following, mean-reversion,
  regime-aware filtering, multi-pair portfolios, and non-technical alpha
  sources including Fear & Greed, funding rate, and DXY), no strategy
  passed the pre-registered out-of-sample gate. The repository includes the
  simulators, data fetchers, datasets, result logs, and the full paper.
keywords:
  - algorithmic trading
  - cryptocurrency
  - backtesting
  - pre-registration
  - out-of-sample validation
  - negative results
  - reproducibility
  - market efficiency
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-05-21"
version: "1.0.0"
